<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  MasterClock — uk (Ukrainian)

  Mode names (Fischer, Byoyomi, Sudden Death…) and chess variant names are Kotlin literals rather
  than resources, so they stay in English by construction — see the notes in values/strings.xml.

  app_name and settings_app_version are left out on purpose: they are the product name.

  Written from the English, not from the Russian. Ukrainian runs longer than English, so the labels
  in tight rows (the settings tabs, the presets tabs, the clock chips) are deliberately short.
  Counted things carry the four plural categories CLDR gives Ukrainian: one, few, many and other
  (other is for fractions, and takes the genitive singular). The apostrophe is the typographic
  one, U+2019, which needs no escaping.

  Translated without a native reviewer, like every language here except the French.
-->
